  "question": {
    "text": "<p>If the maximum value of accelerating potential provided by a radio frequency oscillator is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mi>kV</mi></math>. The number of revolution made by a proton in a cyclotron to achieve&nbsp;one sixth of the speed of light is:&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"\"><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>67</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>19</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, Speed of light<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "543",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>From&nbsp;the conservation of energy,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>19</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>67</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>543</mn></math></p>",
